From 30c4e5bed24099a3bb12840550a7ee43ddaa2656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:04:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fixed point solver with acceleration algorithms (FixedPoint)

New non linear solver `FixedPoint` (FixedPointSolver): iterations
x_{i+1} = x_i - S r(x_i), with
- `Method` = `ElasticOperator` (default): S approximates the inverse of the
  elastic operator K0, assembled from the prediction operators (or the
  elastic operators, `ElasticOperatorComputation` = `Integration`) of the
  behaviours, at each resolution or once (`ElasticOperatorUpdate`), solved
  by the linear solver of the problem or by an own linear solver
  (`ElasticOperatorLinearSolver`), whose setup is kept; the behaviours are
  integrated without tangent operator;
- `Method` = `ModifiedNewton`: tangent operator of the first iteration;
- `Acceleration`: algorithms of the AccelerationAlgorithmFactory, to which
  algorithms can be added; `Anderson` (type II, normal equations updated
  incrementally) and `Cast3M` (as MTest) are declared by default.
The elastic operator given by an operator applied without assembly is its
assembled version.

`HypreBoomerAMG` is also declared as a linear solver (one cycle of
BoomerAMG), for the fixed point on the elastic operator. The log stream
and the printing condition of the Newton solver are moved to
NonLinearSolverBase.

FixedPointSolverTest: methods, accelerations and linear solvers of the
elastic operator give the solution of the Newton solver; accelerations
reduce the number of iterations; the rate of convergence without
acceleration is bounded by 3 mu / (3 mu + H); invalid options are refused.
